From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] riched20: a new editor has no placeholder text

1511 gave the editor a placeholder but never set it when an editor is
made, and the editor is not zeroed: every RichEdit started with whatever
the heap held there. An empty control read it when it drew (an access
violation, swallowed in the window procedure, which stopped the drawing
short) and freed it when it was destroyed. In the QA VM Word crashed on
exit, in editor_draw and in the heap (block_get_type), with or without a
document typed into.

The placeholder is set to none when the editor is made.

Wine's RichEdit editor tests: 14 failures, as before. In the QA VM Word
starts, takes typing and exits without a crash.

Gate: test/richinit-gate.sh (Xvfb; the heap fills new blocks, via
GlobalFlag FLG_HEAP_ENABLE_FREE_CHECK, and the probe counts access
violations). Mutant SG_MUTANT_PLACEHOLDER_UNINIT (riched20/editor.c).
---
--- a/dlls/riched20/editor.c
+++ b/dlls/riched20/editor.c
@@ -2979,6 +2979,11 @@ ME_TextEditor *ME_MakeEditor(ITextHost *texthost, BOOL bEmulateVersion10)
   HDC hdc;
 
   ed->sizeWindow.cx = ed->sizeWindow.cy = 0;
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_PLACEHOLDER_UNINIT
+  /* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 1610): the editor is not zeroed; 1511's
+   * placeholder was left as whatever the heap held, drawn and freed */
+  ed->placeholder = NULL;
+#endif
   if (ITextHost_QueryInterface( texthost, &IID_ITextHost2, (void **)&ed->texthost ) == S_OK)
   {
     ITextHost_Release( texthost );
